===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[occasionally|Occasionally]]; [[sometimes]]; [[once in a while]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:occasionally}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|act=III|scene=iii|text=I'll find out your man, / And he shall signify '''from time to time''' / Every good hap to you that chances here.}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Guy Mannering|chapter=XXV|passage=On these red embers Hatteraick '''from time to time''' threw a handful of twigs.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|chapter=IX|passage=“A tight little craft,” was Austin’s invariable comment on the matron;{{nb...}}. &para; Near her wandered her husband, orientally bland, invariably affable, and '''from time to time''' squinting sideways, as usual, in the ever-renewed expectation that he might catch a glimpse of his stiff, retroussé moustache.}}
#* {{RQ:T. S. Eliot Waste Land|lines=196–197|page=29|passage=But at my back '''from time to time''' I hear / The sound of horns and motors, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=December|author=Cecil J. Allen|title=Operating a mountain main line: the Bern-Lötschberg-Simplon: Part One|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=743|passage='''From time to time''' the coaches of the Lötschberg Railway itself, which in comfort and ''décor'' can rank with the finest in Europe today, travel far from the frontiers of Switzerland on through workings such as these.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|system=PC|scene=Protheans: Data Discs Codex entry|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|passage=Despite all the evidence confirming the existence of the Protheans, little is known about their culture and society. '''From time to time''', dig sites will yield new clues, but after 50,000 years of decay, little of value is unearthed.}}
# {{lb|en|law}} In whatever status exists at various times.{{attention|en|definition may need improved wording}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Richard Painter; Ann Holmes|title=Cases and Materials on Employment Law|page=90
|passage=This is another way of saying that the terms of the individual contracts are in part to be found in the agreed collective agreements as they exist '''from time to time''' {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Continuously from one time to another; at all times, [[constantly]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=III|canto=V|passage=So was she trayned vp '''from time to time''', / In all chast vertue, and true bounti-hed / Till to her dew perfection she was ripened.}}

